    "name": {
      "value": "Cleric"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "crb"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "You are an ordained priest of your deity and have even learned how to cast a few divine spells. Though your main training lies elsewhere, your religious calling provides you divine gifts.\n\n**Multiclass Cleric characters:**\nThe cleric archetype is a great way to create a character of another class who's a devotee of a particular deity. The many domains available to clerics of different deities present a variety of options for focus spells.\n\n- Alchemist clerics work well with the chirurgeon field, healing various ailments with either alchemy or spells.\n- Martial clerics are typically looking for a potent domain spell or some healing to use in a pinch.\n- Divine sorcerer clerics double down as the ultimate divine spellcasters.\n- Other spellcaster clerics diversify their options, becoming theurgic characters who combine two magical traditions."
    },
